sub:Head {
    sub: a np:Nanopublication ;
        np:hasAssertion sub:assertion ;
        np:hasProvenance sub:provenance ;
        np:hasPublicationInfo sub:pubinfo .
}

sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-silvestris-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Drosophila silvestris Turing wavenumber at 2.995 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) faithfully reproduces Drosophila silvestris morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-silvestris-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila silvestris specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-silvestris-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-silvestris-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/drosophila_silvestris_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Drosophila silvestris; environment: python 3.12.3, note numpy, scipy, Pillow, matplotlib. No ~/.nanopub/profile.yml on this runner.; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing (1952) gives the diffusion-driven instability and a critical wavenumber. Schnakenberg (1979) gives the two-species kinetics used here. | Carson & Bryant (1979) report a mean of 20-30 extra tibial cilia in northeast Hawaiian D. silvestris males, absent in D. heteroneura. They do not report a 3 µm wavelength. | Gompel et al. (2005) attribute macroscopic Drosophila wing spots to cis-regulatory evolution.; reconstructed_in_script: Detail-tier wavelength 2.995e-6 m (log10 = -5.524), diffusivity ratio 20, and the chronoseries contrast with D. serrata (9.226e-5 m) and D. simulans (8.256e-5 m) are assigned for this slot and reconstructed from the dispersion relation. | Pass-1 readout is the single loudest Fourier mode of the linearised PDE. Pass-1 mask is every dark foreground pixel.; transfer_boundary: The wavenumber comparison is a scale contrast inside one chronoseries. It does not say that D. serrata or D. simulans evolved into D. silvestris, and it does not transfer to embryonic pair-rule stripes.; does_not_claim: Does not claim the Kilohana wing spots, or the 20-30 extra tibial cilia, are produced by a 2.995 µm Schnakenberg pattern. | Does not claim a second assessor scored this pass. Signing keys were not present.]; phenomenon_size: 1.9 µm (1.919e-06 m, log10=-5.717 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 1.9 µm to 4.3 mm): 1.9 µm:drosophila-affinis-bioelectric-polarity, 6.0 µm:drosophila-affinis-vertex-packing, 96 µm:drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength, 192 µm:drosophila-affinis-clock-wavefront, 432 µm:drosophila-affinis-morphogen-condensation, 528 µm:drosophila-affinis-elastic-buckling, 600 µm:drosophila-affinis-flux-canalization, 840 µm:drosophila-affinis-branching-tree" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(81)90334-9>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature03235>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.76.4.1929>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1179047> .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-silvestris-turing-wavelength-s0.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-silvestris-turing-wavelength-s0.py" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> ;
        schema:programmingLanguage "Python" .
}

